  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 1405.04 Release of Financial Assurance Obligation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 1405.04 Release of Financial Assurance Obligation. An approved financial assurance plan, or any part thereof, shall remain in effect unless:\n\n(a) A facility meets the requirements in Env-Sw 1405.02(d);\n\n(b) The facility is no longer defined as a facility in accordance with Env-Sw 103 and has completed the general closure requirements specified in Env-Sw 1006.02, Env-Sw 1106, Env-Sw 1205, and other rules as applicable; or\n\n(c) The permittee obtains written approval from the department to replace a financial assurance mechanism specified in Env-Sw 1403.03(a), Env-Sw 1403.03(b), Env-Sw 1403.04(b), or Env-Sw 1403.04(c).\n\nSource. #14068, eff 9-3-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1400.html"
